<!-- 📘 CLAUDE.local.md is your PERSONAL, gitignored layer on top of CLAUDE.md. It loads the same
     way but is never committed, so it holds things true for YOU on YOUR machine that should not be
     forced on the team. Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` to use it. We ship the `.example` so
     the pattern is visible without committing a real local file. -->

# Personal overrides (not committed)

## My setup
- I run the dev server on port 4000 (`npm run dev -- -p 4000`).
- My scratch notes for this project are in `~/notes/verdant.md` (don't read it unless I point you there).
- Chromium for Playwright lives at a custom path on this machine:
  `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`. (Leave this unset on a normal laptop,
  where `npx playwright install chromium` downloads the matching browser.)

## My preferences
- When you finish a change, show me the diff before committing.
- I like terse commit messages. No fluff.

## Personal permissions and hooks
Personal permission rules and hook tweaks belong in `.claude/settings.local.json` (also gitignored),
not here. For example, during a live class I silence the memory-nudge Stop hook so it does not
interrupt a demo. Claude Code cannot switch off one hook while keeping it configured, so that hook
reads its own environment variable, and `settings.local.json` sets it:

```json
{
  "env": { "VERDANT_SKIP_MEMORY_NUDGE": "1" }
}
```

Agent teams work the same way, as a personal opt-in:

```json
{
  "env": { "CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS": "1" }
}
```

Agent teams are experimental and terminal-CLI only. We keep that flag OUT of the committed
`.claude/settings.json` on purpose: while it is on, a subagent Claude names launches as a teammate
instead of a plain subagent, which changes the behavior the shared skeleton teaches. Turn it on per
machine here if you want to experiment. (Both keys can sit in the same `env` block.)
